# Static export ships one HTML shell per dynamic route (built for
# placeholder params — see each page.tsx's generateStaticParams under a
# [param] folder). These map every real URL onto the matching shell with a
# 200 (serve, not redirect) so the browser still lands on the real URL; each
# page then reads the true id from window.location itself (see
# src/lib/path-segment.ts) rather than trusting build-time params.
#
# Targets are extensionless on purpose — a target ending in .html fights
# Pages' own built-in .html -> clean-URL redirect and loops.
#
# Placeholder groups (see src/lib/path-segment.ts comment in each layout for
# the fuller reasoning): 'w-root' for the /websites/:id overview page alone,
# 'w-idx' shared by the six index pages that have their own child routes
# (automations, funnels, heatmaps, replays, revenue, settings), 'w-leaf'
# shared by everything else. Different groups exist only to avoid a file and
# a same-named folder colliding on disk — not because the values mean
# anything at runtime.
#
# Passthroughs first: these are real static pages, but they're also single
# path segments — exactly what the :id wildcards below would otherwise
# match, hijacking them. Confirmed necessary by testing (uptime/web hit this
# exact bug with /dashboard/monitors/new).

/websites/manage                              /websites/manage                             200
/websites/:websiteId/automations/new          /websites/w-leaf/automations/new              200
/websites/:websiteId/automations/templates    /websites/w-leaf/automations/templates        200

